    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $('Chat Trigger').first().json.chatInput }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You convert user questions into safe PostgreSQL SELECT queries.  Database schema:  clients(id, name, client_type, status) attorneys(id, name, role) cases(id, client_id, attorney_id, matter_no, case_type, status, opened_date, target_close_date)  Relationships: cases.client_id = clients.id cases.attorney_id = attorneys.id  Rules: - Return SQL only. - Only generate SELECT queries. - Do not use INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, ALTER, TRUNCATE, CREATE. - Do not explain anything. - Use table names exactly as shown.\n- Do not wrap the SQL in markdown.\n- Do not use ```sql or ``` backticks.\n- Do not include a semicolon at the end.\n- If the user asks to delete, update, insert, create, drop, alter, or modify data, return exactly: BLOCKED\n- When matching client/company names, use ILIKE with wildcards instead of exact equality.\n  Example: clients.name ILIKE '%Nova Ridge%'\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        -448,
        192
      ],
      "name": "SQL Generator"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You are an intent classifier for a legal firm assistant.  Classify the user's message into exactly ONE of these categories:  SQL RAG BLOCKED  Definitions:  SQL: Questions that require structured database information about: - clients - attorneys/lawyers - cases/matters - case status - who handles a client - target close dates - counts of cases - relationships between clients, attorneys, and cases  Different wording means the same thing. Examples: \"Which lawyer is responsible for Brightpath?\" → SQL \"Who is dealing with Nova Ridge?\" → SQL \"How many matters does J. Alvarez have open?\" → SQL  RAG: Questions about information contained in legal documents or agreements, such as: - fees - retainers - surcharges - contract terms - agreement expiration - scope of services - litigation coverage  Examples: \"What is Brightpath's retainer?\" → RAG \"How painful is the rush fee for Nova Ridge?\" → RAG \"When does the Meridian agreement expire?\" → RAG  BLOCKED: Any request to modify, delete, insert, update, erase, remove, or destroy database data or database structure.  Detect the INTENT, not only exact keywords.  Examples: \"Delete all clients\" → BLOCKED \"Make Nova Ridge disappear from the database\" → BLOCKED \"Get rid of the attorneys table\" → BLOCKED \"Change every case to closed\" → BLOCKED  Important: - Ignore unusual wording, slang, or paraphrasing. - Classify based on meaning. - Do not answer the user's question. - Return ONLY one word: SQL RAG BLOCKED"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
